    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup configuration, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), whose elite speed profile perfectly aligns with today\u2019s matchup against Jake Irvin. The combination of a favorable park factor and a pitcher allowing a high success rate on stolen base attempts makes **Pete Crow-Armstrong** our priority play for category scarcity. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (77.68) and **Yordan Alvarez** (76.93) provide our highest offensive ceilings. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a slight platoon disadvantage against a lefty in Whisenhunt, his elite xwOBA and favorable wind conditions at the ballpark outweigh the split, solidifying his role in the heart of our order.\n\nBeyond the headliners, we are leveraging significant platoon and matchup advantages. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Christian Yelich** (67.68) draw favorable assignments against right-handed pitching, benefiting from elevated SP-skill projections that inflate their scoring well above their baselines. **Nelson Velazquez** (64.08) is a high-upside play today; the combination of a weak opposing starter in Whisenhunt and wind blowing out boosts his power projection significantly. On the flip side, **Caleb Durbin** (44.54) serves as our most marginal start, as he faces a tier-one arm in Dylan Cease; he remains in the lineup purely to maintain our 5x5 floor while we monitor the impact of Cease's elite pitch profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Carson Benge** (49.17), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Carson Benge** posted a respectable score, the sheer efficiency of our outfield and corner-infield rotation\u2014specifically the platoon-heavy profiles of **Nelson Velazquez** and **Lars Nootbaar**\u2014pushed him out of the starting nine. We continue to monitor the status of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Jacob Gonzalez**, the latter of whom was benched after failing to meet our 40-point efficiency floor against a tough pitcher. Despite a busy day, we are keeping a close eye on the weather and potential lineup shifts for **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** as they face Tanner Bibee, ensuring our game caps are preserved for optimal deployment.",
